  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>Stablecoin market cap rose 2.5% over 30D:</strong> Stablecoin market cap at $302.70B (2.5% higher over 30D) implies fresh dry powder entering crypto rails\u2014usually a constructive backdrop for settlement, trading, and on-chain cash demand. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/09/01/citi-goldman-other-global-banks-and-asset-managers-team-up-on-stablecoin-venture\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Citi, Goldman, other global banks and asset managers team up on stablecoin venture</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Stablecoin market structure remains concentration-led:</strong> leadership is still defined by a small set of large issuers/platforms; share shifts matter as much as aggregate market-cap growth. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/09/01/singapore-proposes-100-reserves-and-a-ban-on-yields-for-stablecoin-issuers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Singapore proposes 100% reserves and a ban on yields for stablecoin issuers</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Bank rails are pushing stablecoins into treasury workflows:</strong> That pushes demand toward treasury and settlement use cases, not only exchange trading liquidity. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/09/01/ethena-pushes-stablecoins-into-everyday-banking-with-high-yield-savings-cards-and-payments\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ethena pushes stablecoins into everyday banking with high-yield savings, cards and payments</a> (CoinDesk).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
